// LEAD (a falling chimney breaks, its top trailing): a length's lean is the rod's plus its LEAD times a share that is 0 at BREAK, 1 at
// LEAD_FULL and goes on beyond it: ((the rod's lean less BREAK) / (LEAD_FULL less BREAK)) to the power LEAD_POW (under 1, rule F1:
// a leading length starts forward at once at the break, a snap); each stops at the lying angle, on the line from the foot to where the rod's top meets the sea. So the
// two lower lengths, which lead, land first and together; the three upper ones have no lead and land at the rod's own second. Each swings a little about
