// ---------- the hour (design 4): ONE smooth law of the journey's second ----------
// The sun's height and bearing are smooth monotone tables of T, set at the entry and at stations: 12 degrees up at bearing 300 at the
// entry (the lighting hour); 7 degrees up where the eye crosses the west-south-west station; at bearing 337.5 where the eye crosses the south-south-east station (there the eye, the stack and the
// low sun stand in one line: the sun goes behind the stack and comes out at its other side); on the horizon where the eye crosses
// the south-east station; 2.6 degrees under where it crosses the east-north-east station; 4 degrees under, due north, from the north-north-west station on, held (the lowest of the white night).
