// ---------- the burn (design 5): ONE driver, the journey's second (the owner's term 1; section 153) ----------
// THE FRONT comes down the stack: its depth under the top is a smooth monotone table of T set at the entry and at stations (never at
// typed seconds), with no slope at the entry. A COURSE'S AGE is T less the second at which the front passed it: PASS, the same table
// read the other way, by depth; the shaders read that table too, so that the sums and the picture go by one law. Above the front a
// course chars over CHAR seconds and keeps flaming until the fall; from SHED_AFTER seconds of age pallets leave its face on true
// parabolas, outward at SHED_OUT m/s at the most. THE CROWN FLAME's height is a second table set at the same places. Nothing of
// this moves while the way stands still. What idles goes by the world's clock, bounded and wrapped at WRAP seconds (every rate is
