// ---------- the fire (design 5): flames, smoke, sparks, the cascade, the pallets of the outline and the ones that are shed ----------
// FLAMES are a covering blend with a colour ramp, never summed: one sleeve of fire round the burnt length (thick at the front, torn
// above it so that the skeleton shows), and TONGUES: upright sheets turned to the eye about the upright, 3 to 6 m tall on every
// burnt course, up to 2.3 times that at the front and 1.875 times while the whole pillar burns, and the crown flame's own on the top; all lean before the wind as they rise.
// THE SLEEVE IS TWO SHELLS (rule F3): the first 0.9 m off the face, the outer one SLEEVE_OFF further: coarser, SLEEVE_THIN the cover, climbing half as fast again, so the two move
// against each other as the eye flies round. A slow great noise (once round the stack, 100 m up it) pushes each shell's noises about by SLEEVE_PUSH of a tile, thickens and thins
